# hack-nerd: the Nerd Fonts build of Hack, its Mono form, whose icons are
# each one cell wide. The font draws the text, Powerline's separators and
# Nerd Fonts' icons, the Font Logos included, and it sets the character
# cell. The set starts at 12 points, 16 pixels at 96 DPI.
#
# check=U+E0B0 is the Powerline arrow, which every Nerd Fonts build holds,
# so it tells the build from a plain font of a similar name.
#
# The Nerd Fonts build holds the icons itself, so the set adds only color
# emoji after it, and GNU Unifont last, which draws every other character.
# vtium ships this font set, never the fonts. Nerd Fonts lists its Font
# Logos icons with no license grant, so no vtium package carries a Nerd
# Fonts file: you install the build yourself. Without it, Unifont draws the
# text and each icon draws as a hollow box.
#
# Licenses: Hack's own work is under MIT, and the glyphs it takes from
# Bitstream Vera under the Bitstream Vera License. Nerd Fonts' patcher is
# under MIT, and its icon sets are under their own licenses: CC-BY-4.0 for
# Font Awesome and Codicons, Apache-2.0 for Material Design Icons, and none
# for Font Logos. The layers name their own licenses.
#
# References:
# - ADR-1204 D3: the Nerd Fonts category.

name=hack-nerd
size=12
license=MIT AND Bitstream-Vera AND OFL-1.1 AND Apache-2.0 AND CC-BY-4.0

# Nerd Fonts 3.4.0's Hack Nerd Font Mono.
source=font:Hack Nerd Font Mono
version=3.4.0
check=U+E0B0
url=https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts/releases/tag/v3.4.0

layer=noto-emoji
layer=unifont
